     aabbttnn — ADB Keyboard Special Keys Driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee aaddbb

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aabbttnn driver provides support for the extended Fn keys on Apple note‐
     books with an ADB interface.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The aabbttnn driver supports extended keyboard keys (special F-keys) on the
     following devices:

     ••   Apple iBook Keyboard
     ••   Apple PowerBook Keyboard

EEVVEENNTTSS
     The aabbttnn driver sends events to devd(8) for the following events under
     the PPMMUU system, and kkeeyyss subsystem:

     ••   bbrriigghhttnneessss - Generates uupp and ddoowwnn notify types matching the pressed
         key.
     ••   mmuuttee
     ••   vvoolluummee - Generates uupp and ddoowwnn notify types matching the pressed key.
     ••   eejjeecctt

     Examples are included in /etc/devd/apple.conf.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     adb(4), akbd(4), cuda(4), pmu(4), devd(8)

